{"event": "model_request", "time": 1793846925.9465113, "run_id": "379adaa030114f95a7f61b156bed8faf", "seq": 12, "number": 1, "body": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Complete the task using the Python tools below.\nReturn ONE JSON object with string fields \"thought\" (next action) and \"code\" (executable Python), then STOP.\nExample: {\"thought\":\"Check progress.\",\"code\":\"print(task_status())\"}\nNo Markdown fences, extra JSON, simulated observations or future turns. Keep the action within the output budget.\n\nCall tools with keyword arguments; arrays are Python lists. Print needed output. Variables and imports persist,\nand successful statements before an error remain executed. Paths are relative to the task repository.\nUse tools for all file/command operations; edit only allowed files, never tests. Use current file_hash as expected_hash.\nImports allowed: ['collections', 'datetime', 'itertools', 'json', 'math', 'queue', 'random', 're', 'stat', 'statistics', 'time', 'unicodedata']; import before use. Read sufficient evidence and avoid repeated unchanged reads.\nWhen the business deliverable is ready, call final_answer: it runs missing current-version verification,\ncompletes the plan on success, or returns the failure for repair. It cannot supply missing reading, baseline or report.\n\nAvailable tools:\n```python\ndef read_file(path: str) -> dict:\n    'Read a text file in full. Returns dict: content (text), file_hash, evidence_ids. Read result[\\'content\\'], not result[:N].\\npath: {\"type\":\"string\"}'\n\ndef read_pdf(start_page: int, end_page: int = None) -> dict:\n    'Read pages using the repository\\'s read_pdf.py helper. Returns dict: pages (list of {page,text}), evidence_ids, delivery. Extract the required range once; complete pages are sent in bounded batches. Queued ids are not yet read. Do not print all pages.\\nstart_page: {\"type\":\"integer\"}\\nend_page: {\"type\":\"integer\"}'\n\ndef run_command(argv: list, cwd: str = None) -> dict:\n    'Run one allowed argv command without a shell. Omit cwd or use \\'.\\' for the task repository root. argv is a Python list[str]. Returns dict: rc, stdout (text), stderr, timed_out.\\nargv: {\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}\\ncwd: {\"type\":\"string\"}'\n\ndef update_plan(items: list) -> dict:\n    'Set the task plan; preserve titles/order and update todo/doing/done.\\nitems: {\"type\":\"array\",\"description\":\"List of objects, e.g. [{\\\\\"title\\\\\":\\\\\"Read sources\\\\\",\\\\\"status\\\\\":\\\\\"doing\\\\\"}]. Each status is todo, doing or done; retain existing titles/order.\"}'\n\ndef recall(evidence_ids: list) -> dict:\n    'Queue evidence ids; batches are bounded and overflow remains pending.\\nevidence_ids: {\"type\":\"array\"}'\n\ndef task_status() -> dict:\n    'Show the current plan, remaining reading, notes, changes and verification, plus evidence ids.'\n\ndef save_answer(section: str, question_id: str, answer: dict, evidence_id: str, page: int, quote: str) -> dict:\n    'Save an answer with exact cited page text. answer must contain exactly value. Returns dict: section, question_id, saved.\\nsection: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\nquestion_id: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\nanswer: {\"type\":\"object\",\"description\":\"{\\'value\\': string, integer or list of strings}\"}\\nevidence_id: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\npage: {\"type\":\"integer\"}\\nquote: {\"type\":\"string\"}'\n\ndef save_section(section: str, summary: str, application: str) -> dict:\n    'Save section prose. Returns dict: section, saved.\\nsection: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\nsummary: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\napplication: {\"type\":\"string\"}'\n\ndef submit_report(overview: str, expected_hash: str) -> dict:\n    'Serialize saved results to report.json. Returns dict: ok, path, before_hash, file_hash, changed.\\noverview: {\"type\":\"string\"}\\nexpected_hash: {\"type\":\"string\"}'\n\ndef write_note(title: str, content: str, evidence_ids: list, section: str) -> dict:\n    'Save or update a literal model-written note grounded in exposed evidence. Returns dict: note_id, sources, chars.\\ntitle: {\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Stable note title; reuse it when updating the same note.\"}\\ncontent: {\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"One contiguous string literal, 20..1500 characters. No adjacent string fragments, concatenation or variable; text must occur verbatim in your response.\"}\\nevidence_ids: {\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"Python list[str], e.g. [\\'ev-abc\\'], not a string. Copy ids from delivered Evidence headers.\"}\\nsection: {\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Required topic: overview/reasoning/tool_use/multi_agent/outlook\"}'\n\ndef final_answer(answer: any) -> any:\n    \"\"\"Provides a final answer to the given problem.\n\n    Args:\n        answer: The final answer to the problem\n    \"\"\"\n\n```"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\nRead the PDF and update report.json.\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"paper\", \"editable\": [\"report.json\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"report.json\"], \"verify_commands\": [[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"]], \"required_pages\": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], \"note_topics\": [\"overview\", \"reasoning\", \"tool_use\", \"multi_agent\", \"outlook\"], \"max_model_calls\": 4}\nUse update_plan before editing and run baseline checks. os and pathlib are unavailable in action code.\nFor write_note, put the complete exact note text in thought and pass the same text as one content string literal in code.\nPaper workflow: Plan, baseline pytest, read report.json and paper.json, then call read_pdf once for the full range. Read the delivered batches; they advance automatically after successful actions. On error use the retained batch. Do not print all pages or reread just to advance.\nIncrementally write_note for each topic, citing delivered evidence ids. Each final note must contain both answers, page numbers and continuous exact quotations supporting every answer item, within 1500 characters. Preserve earlier facts when updating.\nSave each answer via save_answer(section, question_id, answer={'value': ...}, evidence_id, page, quote); save prose via save_section. Choose answers and citations yourself: exact matching proves provenance, not semantic support. Support every array item. After all pages and all five latest notes have appeared together in a later request, call submit_report(overview, expected_hash), then final_answer.\nMulti-agent collaboration and training are future suggestions, not implemented features.\n\nCourse progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"read\",\"next_requirement\":\"PDF pages not yet sent: 1,2,3,4,5\",\"remaining_count\":10,\"requests_left\":3,\"baseline_done\":0,\"changed_files\":[],\"verified_current\":0,\"required_checks\":1,\"request_number\":1,\"max_requests\":4,\"requests_after_response\":3,\"first_write_reading_required\":true,\"full_reads_registered\":{\"report.json\":\"44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a\"},\"evidence_delivery\":\"Registered full reads are logged tool reads; Evidence headers show selected ranges, whose delivery requires HTTP confirmation.\",\"pdf_pages_missing\":[1,2,3,4,5]}\nEvidence ev-0bb88db782dbb846de19 | report.json | lines:1-1 | sha256=44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a\n{}\nEvidence ev-43852c44687baca48e12 | paper.pdf | page:1 | sha256=1b7371417f2dc7bd2b4d16ec6f63bbe53d72dfb4d5c10ef42c2ce9d5394aca5c\nObserved PDF page 0 with substantive text.\nEvidence ev-4609a2662ec458fe5e71 | paper.pdf | page:2 | sha256=1b7371417f2dc7bd2b4d16ec6f63bbe53d72dfb4d5c10ef42c2ce9d5394aca5c\nObserved PDF page 1 with substantive text.\nEvidence ev-c86a87a1f4e38c6715bf | paper.pdf | page:3 | sha256=1b7371417f2dc7bd2b4d16ec6f63bbe53d72dfb4d5c10ef42c2ce9d5394aca5c\nObserved PDF page 2 with substantive text.\nEvidence ev-82ae75f5539e2e6ba21d | paper.pdf | page:4 | sha256=1b7371417f2dc7bd2b4d16ec6f63bbe53d72dfb4d5c10ef42c2ce9d5394aca5c\nObserved PDF page 3 with substantive text.\nEvidence ev-e8bfd076b2d75736f2e6 | paper.pdf | page:5 | sha256=1b7371417f2dc7bd2b4d16ec6f63bbe53d72dfb4d5c10ef42c2ce9d5394aca5c\nObserved PDF page 4 with substantive text."}]}], "model": "deepseek-flash", "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}, "stop": ["Observation:", "Calling tools:"]}, "chars": 8336, "content_chars": 7762, "course_content_chars": 8165}
